<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia raises 69.5 million dinars at auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisia raises 69.5 million dinars at auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury on Tuesday raised 69.5 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury bills dated June 17, and repaid maturing paper totalling 47.2 million dinars.</p>
<p>Herewith breakdown of the results:</p>
<p>  Maturity			 Amount     Rate     Previous rate</p>
<p>- Two-year notes payable</p>
<p> in equal annual tranches     12 MD    6.9375	 7.0000</p>
<p>				     41.5MD    7.0000	     -</p>
<p>- Two-year note payable at maturity</p>
<p>				    10 MD     6.8750	    6.8750</p>
<p>				     5 MD     6.9375	    6.9375</p>
<p>				     1 MD     7.0000		-</p>
<p>Banks bid for 171 million dinars for two, three and five-year paper at between 6.8750 and 8.0625 percent.</p>
<p>(one $=1.0994 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
